# A ring inside a package, panel 252's R1 (2026-11-19): the package
# `ringlib`, fetched and placed in `heroes.packages/` at the fingerprint its
# catalogue entry names, has a face `shapes` that uses `shapes/internal/calc`,
# and the private module names and builds the face's own record, the shape
# Rebel's packages wrote mirrors to avoid. A 5 by 6 rectangle: area 30,
# doubled width 10.
use <ringlib>/shapes

function main()
    r = shapes.Rect(w: 5, h: 6)
    print(shapes.area(r: r), " ", shapes.doubled(r: r).w)
